}

body:json {
  {
    "send": false,
    "ignoreSchedule": false
  }
}

docs {
  # Pending Approval Reminder (Manual)

  Manually runs the daily pending-approval reminder job. By default this is a
  **preview** — it returns who would be notified and the exact message, and sends nothing.

  ## Access
  SuperUser only. Returns 403 for all other roles.

  ## Body
  | Field            | Type    | Default | Description |
  |------------------|---------|---------|-------------|
  | `send`           | boolean | `false` | `false` = preview only (nothing sent). `true` = actually send the push notifications. |
  | `ignoreSchedule` | boolean | `false` | `false` = only people due a reminder today (same as the cron). `true` = everyone holding overdue tickets. |

  ⚠️ `"send": true` sends real notifications to real users.

  ## Who is reminded
  Only the people currently holding a ticket nobody has acted on:

  - **Stage 1 — requestor's department:** HOD step still pending (`hodStatus = "--"`)
    → the requestor's HOD only (not the RM, not the assigned department).
  - **Stage 2 — assigned department:** requestor's HOD has approved / forwarded and
    RM, HOD and DeptHOD of the assigned department are all still pending
    → RM + HOD + DeptHOD of the assigned department.
    (If the ticket was raised to the requestor's own department → DeptHOD only.)

  Only tickets with status `Open` are considered — Checking, Pending Acknowledgement,
  Broadcast and closed tickets are skipped. The requestor is never reminded about their own ticket.

  ## Timing
  - Calendar days (Sundays and holidays count).
  - First reminder after **3 full days** in the current stage.
    Stage 2 counts from the HOD approval / forward date, not the ticket creation date.
  - Then repeated on **alternate days** (day 3, 5, 7 …) until someone acts.
  - Each person gets **one** notification with their total ticket count.

  ## Automatic schedule
  The same job runs automatically via cron every day at **10:00 AM IST**.

  ## Notification content
  - Title: "⏰ Reminder: 15 tickets awaiting your approval"
    (1 ticket → "⏰ Reminder: 1 ticket awaiting your approval")
  - Body: none — the notification shows the title only, with the RTS logo
  - type / action: `pending_approval_reminder`
  - channel_id: `rts_notifications`
  - requireInteraction: true

  ## What happens on tap
  `url` = `/?pendingApprovals=1` → the web dashboard opens the **Pending Approvals** popup:
  one small card per role + dept with the number of pending tickets
  (data from `GET /requests/pending-approvals`, see 02-Requests → Pending Approvals).
  Tapping a card switches to that role (if needed) and shows only those tickets
  (a single ticket opens its details). If the user was logged out, they land on the
  popup right after login.

  Management (GN-01 / GN-02) → `url` = `/management` (they approve in the Management portal).

  Mobile (FCM data): `type` / `action` = `pending_approval_reminder`, `pending_count`,
  `deepLink` = `FRONTEND_URL + /?pendingApprovals=1`.
  A native app should open its own pending list screen by calling `GET /requests/pending-approvals`.

  > 📱 Sent to **web push + mobile app** (default).
  > To pause mobile for this reminder only: set `PENDING_REMINDER_MOBILE=false` in the backend `.env` and restart.
  > (New-ticket and other notifications are not affected by this setting.)

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "sent": false,
    "ignoreSchedule": false,
    "count": 1,
    "recipients": [
      {
        "empId": "GN-1042",
        "name": "Sudhakar G Hegde",
        "own": 12,
        "assigned": 3,
        "oldest": 131,
        "title": "⏰ Reminder: 15 tickets awaiting your approval"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  - `own` — tickets from the person's own department awaiting their HOD approval
  - `assigned` — tickets assigned to their department awaiting approval
  - `oldest` — days the longest-pending ticket has waited
}
